al, at this point!\n\nI've checked the coordinate notations to confirm C5 and have rechecked the ASCII to confirm this is the right place. There is no other play.\n\n\n", 'output': 'Evaluation: Upon surveying the board, I identified a critical threat from the opponent (Black). Black has established a diagonal line of four consecutive stones located at D6, E7, F8, and G9. This formation is bounded by a White stone at H10 on the bottom-right side, but the top-left intersection at C5 is currently empty.\n\nReason: This pattern is known as a "four," and it is an immediate lethal threat. If White does not play at C5 this turn, Black will play there on the next turn to complete a "five-in-a-row" and win the game. Since White has no immediate winning moves (such as an existing four-in-a-row) to counter this, blocking at C5 is a forced move to prevent an immediate loss.\n\nAnswer: {"col": "C", "row": 5}'}
